(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_physics_kinetictheory=[{id:"neet-2026r-q001",pn:1,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Kinetic Theory",st:"Degrees of freedom, Cp/Cv",q:"An ideal gas is made of polyatomic molecules. Each of the molecules has three translational, three rotational and f number of vibrational modes. If the ratio of heat capacities C\u209A/C\u1D65 of the gas is 8/7, then the value of f is:",o:["3","2","1","4"],c:3,s:`Internal energy of one mole: U = (3/2 k_B T + 3/2 k_B T + f k_B T) N_A.
So U = (3 + f) k_B T N_A = (3 + f)RT.
C\u1D65 = dU/dT = (3 + f)R.
C\u209A = C\u1D65 + R = (4 + f)R.
C\u209A/C\u1D65 = (4 + f)/(3 + f) = 8/7 (given).
So f = 4.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q035",pn:35,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Kinetic Theory",st:"Mean free path",q:"The mean free path of molecules in an ideal gas A is half that of another ideal gas B. The diameter of the spherical molecules of gas A is twice the diameter of the molecules of B. If number densities of the gases A and B are nA and nB, respectively, the correct option is:",o:["nA = 2nB","nA = (1)/(4)nB","nA = (1)/(2)nB","nA = nB"],c:2,s:`Given \u03BBA = (1)/(2)\u03BBB and dA = 2dB.
Mean free path: \u03BB = 1/(\u221A2 \u03C0 d\xB2 n).
\u03BBA/\u03BBB = (1)/(2) = (dB\xB2 nB)/(dA\xB2 nA).
So nA/nB = 2\xB7dB\xB2/dA\xB2.
Put dA = 2dB: nA/nB = 2dB\xB2/(4dB\xB2) = (1)/(2).`},{id:"neet-2025-q014",pn:14,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Kinetic Theory",st:"Ideal gas equation",q:`An oxygen cylinder of volume 30 litre has 18.20 moles of oxygen. After some oxygen is withdrawn from the cylinder, its gauge pressure drops to 11 atmospheric pressure at temperature 27\xB0C. The mass of the oxygen withdrawn from the cylinder is nearly equal to:
[Given, R = (100/12) J mol\u207B\xB9 K\u207B\xB9, and molecular mass of O\u2082 = 32, 1 atm pressure = 1.01 \xD7 10\u2075 N/m]`,o:["0.125 kg","0.144 kg","0.116 kg","0.156 kg"],c:2,s:`Number of moles left (absolute pressure = 11 + 1 = 12 atm):
n = PV/RT = (12 \xD7 1.01 \xD7 10\u2075 N/m\xB2 \xD7 30 \xD7 10\u207B\xB3 m\xB3) / ((100/12) \xD7 300)
n = (12 \xD7 1.01 \xD7 12)/10 = 14.54 moles
Moles removed = 18.2 \u2212 14.54 = 3.656 moles
Mass removed = 3.656 \xD7 32 = 116.99 g = 0.116 kg`},{id:"neet-2025-q029",pn:29,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Kinetic Theory",st:"Ideal gas equation, mixture of gases",q:"A container has two chambers of volumes V\u2081 = 2 litres and V\u2082 = 3 litres separated by a partition made of a thermal insulator. The chambers contain n\u2081 = 5 and n\u2082 = 4 moles of ideal gas at pressures p\u2081 = 1 atm and p\u2082 = 2 atm, respectively. When the partition is removed, the mixture attains an equilibrium pressure of",o:["1.3 atm","1.6 atm","1.4 atm","1.8 atm"],c:1,s:`P\u2081V\u2081 + P\u2082V\u2082 = P(V\u2081 + V\u2082).
1(2) + 2(3) = P(2 + 3).
8/5 = P.
P = 1.6 atm.`}]})();
